/* 

  Logistic distribution in Picat.

  From 
  https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Logistic_distribution
  """
  Quantile function
  The inverse cumulative distribution function (quantile function) of the 
  logistic distribution is a generalization of the logit function. Its derivative is 
  called the quantile density function. They are defined as follows:
    Q(p;mu,s) = mu + s * ln(p/(1-p))
    Q(p;s)    = s/(p*(1-p))
  """

  See ppl_distributions.pi and ppl_distributions_test.pi for more on this

  Picat> X = logistic_dist_mean()
  X = 0


  Picat> X = logistic_dist_mean(3,1)
  X = 3

  Cf my Gamble model gamble_logistic_dist.rkt


  This program was created by Hakan Kjellerstrand, hakank@gmail.com
  See also my Picat page: http://www.hakank.org/picat/

*/

import ppl_distributions, ppl_utils.
import util.
% import ordset.

main => go.

